    "rule": "saea-mf10-within-intent-card-derangement-v1: an intent's carded types are rotated among THEMSELVES, so that intent's block holds the same MULTISET of vocabularies and is token-matched by construction rather than by a cap. The mapping is per intent for exactly this reason -- one global map would carry an intent's rotation into another intent that shares a type and break the match. An intent listing a single carded type cannot rotate in place, and neither can a carded type no block lists at all; both are pooled and rotated among themselves, as KU-S3's derangement does for its singleton scenario buckets, and the volume difference that leaves is reported as a covariate rather than claimed as a match",
